  A funny textbook example of use-mention error came up today in English
(well, Yeshivish) in our Talmud study.  We are studying the tractate of
"Avodah Zorah" ("Idol Worship"), and our rabbi said, "Sometimes, when you
feel excitement building in you and you don't know what it is, it's 'Avodah
Zorah'" (https://youtu.be/zbg4xenUuuM?t=1048) He immediately retracted it,
because although he meant "di'inaiku do cinmo lo banro terfra be ne'i do ku
gi'e  na djuno lo du'u by du makau .i by nu co'e la'e lu nu malceisni
cesri'isi'a li'u " but it sounded like he meant "li'o by za'i malceisni
cesri'isi'a"

               --gejyspa



